{"family":"recover","task":"flow","name":"ReCoVEr","plain":"ReCoVEr (TU Darmstadt, 2025): optical flow without a cost volume, so it is fast and light at high resolution; three sizes. BSD-3-Clause code and weights; some training sets are research-only.","summary":"ReCoVEr (Kiefhaber, Roth & Schaub-Meyer, ICCV 2025): optical flow without a cost volume. SEA-RAFT's update block refines a flow regressed from a context encoder on both frames (6 channels, stride 8); the authors' training removes the correlation input, so no feature encoder and no correlation pyramid run at inference. 4 iterations, convex upsampling. The authors' released weights; the network is ported from visinf/ReCoVEr. Three context encoders: `recover-cx` (ConvNeXt-T stages, most accurate), `recover-rn` (ResNet34 stages), `recover-mn` (MobileNetV3-Large, fastest). Paper: CX reaches state-of-the-art accuracy at 1.2x the speed and 1/6 the memory of comparable models; MN runs Full HD at 20 FPS in 500 MB.","tier":"experimental","upstream":"https://github.com/visinf/ReCoVEr","upstream_commit":"503a27e38bad1080bd29da91df74c5523e11f8d8","original_is":null,"papers":[{"title":"Removing Cost Volumes from Optical Flow Estimators","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.13317","date":"2025-10-15","venue":"ICCV 2025","variants":[]}],"official":[],"modes":["portable","kernels"],"portable_dtype":"float16","kernels_dtype":"float16","kernel_libs":["cudnn_hacc"],"mps_kernel_libs":[],"mps_dtypes":["float32"],"no_kernels_reason":"","options":[{"name":"iters","default":4,"bounds":">= 1","effect":"output"}],"outputs":[{"name":"flow","extra":false}],"output_info":{},"licence_files":["LICENSE"],"licence_notes":[],"limitations":[],"task_io":"Input: two RGB images (consecutive frames). Output: per-pixel motion from the first to the second (dx, dy in pixels).","install":{"extras":[],"noncommercial_weights":[]},"variants":[{"id":"recover-cx","released":null,"added_in":"0.2.0","ref":"recover-cx@1","name":"recover-cx","setting":"","defaul